<h2>Where should the filters sit on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Each option has the same three filters: event type, failed sign-ins, and a date range (one week or any range within the 90 days). Wireframes only; the real styling will use the guideline tokens.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter bar above the table</h3>
      <p>All controls are always visible in one row that wraps on narrow screens. Labels sit above each control. The result count is under the bar.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;align-items:flex-end">
            <div><div class="label">Show</div>
              <div style="display:flex;gap:6px">
                <button class="mock-button">All events</button>
                <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins</button>
                <button class="mock-button">Security changes</button>
              </div></div>
            <div><div class="label">Event type</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="All types (select)"></div>
            <div><div class="label">From</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="date"></div>
            <div><div class="label">To</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="date"></div>
            <div><div class="label">Range</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Last 7 days (select)"></div>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:10px 0 4px">Showing 6 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When / Event / Device / Location / IP / Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Quick-filter chips plus a "More filters" popover</h3>
      <p>The common cases are one click away. Event type and dates live in a popover. Active filters appear as removable tags above the table.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">
            <button class="mock-button">All events</button>
            <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins</button>
            <button class="mock-button">Security changes</button>
            <button class="mock-button">More filters</button>
          </div>
          <div style="margin-top:8px;display:flex;gap:6px">
            <span class="mock-button">Sep 22 to Sep 28 x</span>
            <span class="mock-button">Sign-in failed x</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:10px 0 4px">Showing 3 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When / Event / Device / Location / IP / Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Event-type checklist in a side column</h3>
      <p>All nine types are visible as checkboxes in a fieldset beside the table, with dates above the list. The table loses width, and the column stacks above the table on narrow screens.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="display:flex;gap:12px">
          <div class="mock-sidebar" style="min-width:150px">
            <div class="label">Dates</div>
            <div>From [date]</div><div>To [date]</div>
            <div class="label" style="margin-top:8px">Event type</div>
            <div>[x] Sign-in</div><div>[x] Sign-in failed</div><div>[x] Sign-out</div>
            <div>[x] Session expired</div><div>[x] Password changed</div>
            <div>[x] Two-factor enabled</div><div>[x] Email change requested</div>
            <div>[x] Settings updated</div><div>[x] API token used</div>
          </div>
          <div style="flex:1">
            <p style="margin:0 0 4px">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
            <div class="placeholder">Table</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
